      "rev_n_1_96a4d3_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_96a4d3_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_96a4d3",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of checking each possible substring for reversibility is inefficient and can miss optimal solutions. Instead, we should focus on identifying the first character that can be improved by reversing a substring starting from it. This approach will be more efficient and likely to find the correct solution in most cases.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_96a4d3_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_9c16b16443",
        "created_at": 1794531316.53789
      },
      "rev_n_2_d5da6f_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_d5da6f_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_d5da6f",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of looking for adjacent characters where swapping would make the string lexicographically smaller is not sufficient. It fails for cases where reversing a longer substring can lead to a lexicographically smaller string. We need to consider all possible substrings and check if reversing any of them can result in a lexicographically smaller string. This approach would be more comprehensive but also more computationally expensive.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_d5da6f_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_433a505633",
        "created_at": 1794531339.0380266
      },
      "rev_n_3_ee1a02_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_ee1a02_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_ee1a02",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of reversing substrings of increasing length from the beginning of the string is inefficient and may miss the optimal solution. Instead, we should consider reversing substrings that contain the first character that can be made lexicographically smaller. This approach ensures we find the lexicographically smallest string possible by a single reversal.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_ee1a02_0",
